1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,067
In this video you will update Kefir, the Kefir Hub app itself and the system

2
00:00:05,067 --> 00:00:08,467
firmware, and see how to handle a downgrade safely.

3
00:00:08,467 --> 00:00:11,933
Press R to switch to the Tools tab and open Updater.

4
00:00:11,933 --> 00:00:17,533
The console needs an internet connection: the version list is downloaded every time.

5
00:00:17,533 --> 00:00:19,667
At the top there are four lines.

6
00:00:19,667 --> 00:00:24,200
Current Kefir and Latest Kefir show your version and the newest one.

7
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:27,667
Current Firmware is the system the console runs now.

8
00:00:27,667 --> 00:00:29,667
Console says Erista or Mariko.

9
00:00:29,667 --> 00:00:32,533
Below are two sections, KEFIR and FIRMWARE.

10
00:00:32,533 --> 00:00:37,000
A version newer than yours is tagged UPDATE, a lower one DOWNGRADE.

11
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:40,667
A firmware your Kefir cannot run is tagged Unsupported.

12
00:00:40,667 --> 00:00:43,867
If the list did not load, press X to refresh it.

13
00:00:43,867 --> 00:00:45,867
Let's start with Kefir.

14
00:00:45,867 --> 00:00:50,267
In the KEFIR section select the version tagged UPDATE and press A.

15
00:00:50,267 --> 00:00:55,200
A window opens with the changes between your version and the selected one.

16
00:00:55,200 --> 00:00:57,467
Scroll to the end with D-pad down.

17
00:00:57,467 --> 00:00:59,467
L and R scroll a page.

18
00:00:59,467 --> 00:01:03,133
The install button unlocks only when you reach the end.

19
00:01:03,133 --> 00:01:06,400
Press down once more, select Install and press A.

20
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:10,867
If you change your mind, press B: nothing is downloaded until then.

21
00:01:10,867 --> 00:01:15,267
Kefir Hub downloads the package and unpacks it to the memory card.

22
00:01:15,267 --> 00:01:19,067
The payload and the bootloader files are updated with it.

23
00:01:19,067 --> 00:01:22,000
At the end you see "Kefir package installed.

24
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Reboot now?".

25
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:27,733
Choose Reboot, or Later if you want to restart yourself.

26
00:01:27,733 --> 00:01:33,000
After the reboot the update finishes by itself, you do not need to do anything.

27
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:35,000
Now the firmware.

28
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:40,333
A firmware install writes to the console's system storage, so first a few rules.

29
00:01:40,333 --> 00:01:45,333
Keep the console on the charger and do not power it off during the install.

30
00:01:45,333 --> 00:01:47,333
Back up your saves first.

31
00:01:47,333 --> 00:01:52,733
Do not keep your own files in the firmware folder on the card: it is replaced and

32
00:01:52,733 --> 00:01:54,733
then deleted.

33
00:01:54,733 --> 00:01:59,867
On top of the firmware archive, keep at least 300 MB free on the memory card.

34
00:01:59,867 --> 00:02:05,467
Custom system themes and system interface translations are deleted on every firmware

35
00:02:05,467 --> 00:02:07,467
install.

36
00:02:07,467 --> 00:02:09,867
Install them again after the update.

37
00:02:09,867 --> 00:02:13,400
In the FIRMWARE section select a version and press A.

38
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:18,133
If your Kefir does not support it, Kefir Hub first offers Update Kefir.

39
00:02:18,133 --> 00:02:22,000
Accept it, and the firmware download continues afterwards.

40
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:24,000
Confirm Download.

41
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:27,667
After the download Kefir Hub checks the firmware files.

42
00:02:27,667 --> 00:02:30,400
If the check fails, nothing is installed.

43
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:35,867
The install prompt shows the version and the target: sysMMC, the internal storage,

44
00:02:35,867 --> 00:02:37,867
or emuMMC.

45
00:02:37,867 --> 00:02:41,333
The firmware goes to the system you are running now.

46
00:02:41,333 --> 00:02:43,333
Check this line.

47
00:02:43,333 --> 00:02:45,333
Choose Install and wait.

48
00:02:45,333 --> 00:02:47,333
Do not power off the console.

49
00:02:47,333 --> 00:02:52,667
At the end Kefir Hub tells you that custom themes and translations were removed.

50
00:02:52,667 --> 00:02:54,667
Choose Reboot.

51
00:02:54,667 --> 00:02:58,200
The downloaded firmware files are deleted afterwards.

52
00:02:58,200 --> 00:03:02,933
If the firmware is already on the memory card, select Install manually.

53
00:03:02,933 --> 00:03:06,867
A file browser opens with the title Select firmware folder.

54
00:03:06,867 --> 00:03:11,400
For a folder, open it and select the top row, Select current folder.

55
00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:15,200
For a zip archive, select the archive itself and press A.

56
00:03:15,200 --> 00:03:17,200
Confirm with Select.

57
00:03:17,200 --> 00:03:20,333
Then the same check and the same prompt follow.

58
00:03:20,333 --> 00:03:25,600
After an install from a folder or an archive Kefir Hub asks what to do with the

59
00:03:25,600 --> 00:03:27,600
source files: Keep or Delete.

60
00:03:27,600 --> 00:03:29,600
Keep is selected by default.

61
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:34,067
A downgrade means installing a lower firmware than the current one.

62
00:03:34,067 --> 00:03:39,400
When you select a version tagged DOWNGRADE, the Firmware downgrade warning opens

63
00:03:39,400 --> 00:03:41,400
first.

64
00:03:41,400 --> 00:03:45,600
Careful: in this window the confirm button is already selected.

65
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:47,933
Pressing A continues the downgrade.

66
00:03:47,933 --> 00:03:49,933
Press B to cancel.

67
00:03:49,933 --> 00:03:54,333
What happens after a downgrade is set by the Downgrade fix option.

68
00:03:54,333 --> 00:03:56,333
Press Plus in the Updater.

69
00:03:56,333 --> 00:04:01,933
Automatic prepares the fix without asking, Optional (ask) asks every time, Off never

70
00:04:01,933 --> 00:04:03,933
applies it.

71
00:04:03,933 --> 00:04:08,933
The fix deletes the system save 8000000000000073 and runs in TegraExplorer.

72
00:04:08,933 --> 00:04:14,533
So after a downgrade with the fix the console restarts into TegraExplorer instead of

73
00:04:14,533 --> 00:04:16,533
a normal reboot.

74
00:04:16,533 --> 00:04:21,867
The TegraExplorer screen appears, does its work by itself and returns you to the

75
00:04:21,867 --> 00:04:23,867
firmware.

76
00:04:23,867 --> 00:04:25,867
But this is not guaranteed.

77
00:04:25,867 --> 00:04:27,867
Warning!

78
00:04:27,867 --> 00:04:33,400
If the firmware still does not boot after a downgrade, Maintenance Mode is the only

79
00:04:33,400 --> 00:04:35,400
way.

80
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:37,933
The steps are also in the warning box.

81
00:04:37,933 --> 00:04:39,933
Power on the console.

82
00:04:39,933 --> 00:04:42,667
After the Kefir logo the trident appears.

83
00:04:42,667 --> 00:04:47,867
As soon as it does, hold both volume buttons and keep holding: the blue-yellow

84
00:04:47,867 --> 00:04:52,400
Atmosphère logo appears, then the sloth logo, then Maintenance Mode.

85
00:04:52,400 --> 00:04:56,067
Choose "Initialize Console Without Deleting Save Data".

86
00:04:56,067 --> 00:04:58,933
The wording depends on the system language.

87
00:04:58,933 --> 00:05:02,067
All games are gone and must be installed again.

88
00:05:02,067 --> 00:05:04,933
Profiles, most settings and all saves stay.

89
00:05:04,933 --> 00:05:09,800
When the console offers to delete the Nintendo folder on the card, agree.

90
00:05:09,800 --> 00:05:13,400
The QR code in the box opens a manual downgrade guide.

91
00:05:13,400 --> 00:05:16,200
What is left is updating Kefir Hub itself.

92
00:05:16,200 --> 00:05:21,400
It checks for a new version once, when it starts, so it needs internet at that

93
00:05:21,400 --> 00:05:23,400
moment.

94
00:05:23,400 --> 00:05:27,067
The behaviour is set in Settings, General, Auto-update.

95
00:05:27,067 --> 00:05:29,267
When to install has three values.

96
00:05:29,267 --> 00:05:31,267
Off never checks.

97
00:05:31,267 --> 00:05:36,800
Silent downloads in the background, and the next launch opens the new version; this

98
00:05:36,800 --> 00:05:38,800
is the default.

99
00:05:38,800 --> 00:05:40,800
Ask shows a prompt.

100
00:05:40,800 --> 00:05:44,933
With Ask, this appears at launch: "A new version is available.

101
00:05:44,933 --> 00:05:46,933
Update now?".

102
00:05:46,933 --> 00:05:48,933
Later asks again next time.

103
00:05:48,933 --> 00:05:52,200
Skip this update stops asking about this version.

104
00:05:52,200 --> 00:05:54,667
Update downloads and installs it now.

105
00:05:54,667 --> 00:05:57,067
When it finishes, restart Kefir Hub.

106
00:05:57,067 --> 00:06:00,933
The Update now item in the settings does the same by hand.

107
00:06:00,933 --> 00:06:05,333
Read more on the Updater and Settings pages of the Kefir Hub docs.
